                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a nice little platformer, but sadly it felt like an average game to me. I mean, it works, it doesn't crash, it has unconventional story, it has smooth controls. But it's missing the feature which could make it a gem or excellent game. The camera could be a bit smoother, the speed of game could be a bit slower (though you quickly get used to it). Some sounds are funny and most of them feel appropriate. Music is ok. At the moment of writing this review, I didn't finish the whole game yet (stopped just at the end of world 4, world 5 is the last one). I might update this review after I finish the game, but I doubt it will change much.\n\n[b]Some suggestions:[/b] I would add world selection with cumulative coins numbers (so that the coins you've already collected doesn't appear and you need to find only the missing ones) instead of how it is implemented now, where you need to restart the whole game if you missed just 1 coin in let's say world 5. But that's a minor detail.\nIt would be also nice if the rock falling down could collide with enemies (so that you could kill enemy indirectly) - it's a very tiny detail, which most players might not even notice during their play-through, but it would feel great when you see that happening for yourself. More interaction with environment would help the game in general.\n\n[b]A few words about developer:[/b] The developer is active on SteamGifts forums and is a very nice person in overall. Of course, it doesn't influence the current state of the game directly, but he's listening to what players think about the game and even made a small competition-event based on the game with some huge prizes for participants. At the moment the new one is going on, so you might consider participating if you get the game: https://www.steamgifts.com/discussion/Xcy2g/summer-goblin-and-coins-marathon\n\n[b]Last words:[/b] It's a pure platforming game which doesn't bring many new or interesting ideas, but it does its platforming part pretty well and gives some funny moments as a bonus. Be ready that the game is on a hard side of difficulty. For the low price it has: it's totally worth it if you enjoy platformers.",
